  "description": "Our double-speed BACKROAD AL GRX RX810 really kicks up a storm, shining through the dust with its sensitive handling. Off-road bikers get to enjoy the complete package: Carbon fork, a stiff, resilient frame with ground and filled welds in carbon look and disc brakes with 12mm thru axles at the front and rear. Fully integrated cables create a clean style, yet the bike can be easily maintained – handlebar, stem and spacer can be replaced without disconnecting them. The bike is equipped with Shimano’s top gravel groupset GRX RX810, which works as precisely as a road group and as robustly as a mountain bike group. The 2x11 gears provide sensitive handling and plenty of gear range for a feeling of well-being between dust and asphalt. All it takes is a twitch of your finger – kick it into high gear and go gravel! The GRX groupsets are specially designed for gravel and cross bikes. They feature the Shadow RD+ Technology with its many advantages: Thanks to the intelligent construction, they offer better protection from damage and prevent chain slaps efficiently, therefore ensuring precise and reliable gear shifts even in rough terrain. * approx. 9.4 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for roasted olive frame, 57 cm, without pedals",
